        <body>
            <div xml:id="d234">

                <pb facs="0375" n="203" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg203"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 857.857/119</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Cardiff</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lathrop</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cardiff</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 4, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 8 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Frederick Kragel, American fireman, Norwegian unarmed
                    steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Sandvik</hi>, Goole, England, to Göteborg, cargo
                    iron and iron ore, reports vessel sunk by submarine believed German, about noon,
                    27th, <pb facs="0376" n="204" xml:id="pg204"/> 5 miles off Aberdeen. Warned,
                    sank in 15 minutes after crew left. Weather clear, cold. Sea rough. Wind high.
                    No vessel in sight. No passengers. Crew rescued after two hours by British mine
                    sweeper and landed Aberdeen. No casualties.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lathrop</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
